.TH WELLDOCTOR 1 "September 2026" "wellutils 1.4.0-54" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
welldoctor \- system health check
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B welldoctor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs read-only checks and prints one status line per check plus a summary:
S.M.A.R.T. health of fixed disks, CPU temperature thresholds, root
filesystem usage, failed systemd units, leftover package-manager config files
(.pacnew/.pacsave, .dpkg-*, .rpmnew/.rpmsave, .apk-new, ._cfg*) and orphan
packages.
.PP
S.M.A.R.T. is read with
.BR smartctl (8)
and needs root or passwordless sudo; otherwise the check is reported as
unavailable. A disk is critical only when smartctl reports a failed overall
health self-assessment. Failed-unit checks are skipped (reported as
unavailable) when systemd is not PID 1, e.g. inside containers.
.PP
Designed for cron/systemd timers: the exit code reflects the worst finding,
in every output mode (plain, box,
.BR \-\-json ", " \-\-short ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
Warnings found.
.TP
.B 2
Critical findings (failing S.M.A.R.T., temperature >= 85C, root fs >= 90%),
or invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Runtime error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
welldoctor && echo OK || echo "check your mail"
welldoctor --json | jq .summary
welldoctor --short          # e.g. "OK 100/100" or "FAIR 90/100 (W1)"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR pacdiff (8),
.BR wellutils (1)
